es == ['home content\\n']. \u2713\n\nAnd expandvars test: '$PYTUTILS_TEST_DIR/islurp_var.txt' with env var = str(tmp_path). expandvars \u2192 str(tmp_path) + '/islurp_var.txt'. File created there. \u2713\n\nWait, one gotcha: os.path.expandvars on '$VAR' \u2014 if VAR is set, expands. monkeypatch.setenv sets os.environ. \u2713\n\nAnother gotcha for expanduser test: os.path.expanduser checks `os.environ['HOME']` \u2014 monkeypatch.setenv modifies os.environ. \u2713 On POSIX. Also set USERPROFILE for Windows. Note: on Windows, expanduser path uses both; setting both is harmless.\n\nHmm, also for the no-expanduser test: I monkeypatch.setenv('HOME', str(tmp_path / 'no-such-home')) so that IF expansion happened, open('no-such-home/f.txt') fails. And expandvars default True \u2014 '~/f.txt' no '$'. \u2713. And I chdir to tmp_path so '~/f.txt' resolves to tmp_path/~/f.txt. Need mkdir '~' and write file. \u2713\n\nWait, one more subtlety: `monkeypatch.chdir(tmp_path)` \u2014 after test, monkeypatch restores CWD. \u2713\n\nFor the dash-no-stdin test: chdir to tmp_path (empty) so open('-') definitely fails. Also, expandvars('-') = '-', expanduser('-') = '-'. open('-') \u2192 FileNotFoundError. \u2713\n\nHmm, should the dash-no-stdin test also verify that stdin was NOT consumed? Could assert sys.stdin untouched \u2014 meh, skip. Actually, a nice postcondition: the error is raised (file '-' not found) \u2014 that IS the assertion. \u2713\n\nLet me also think about whether `list()` on the generator inside pytest.raises works: the generator raises on first next() \u2192 list propagates. \u2713\n\nNow \u2014 the stdin test once more. In the BROKEN world: `list(generator)` \u2192 first next() \u2192 line 40 \u2192 UnboundLocalError. Caught. assert fake_stdin is sys.stdin \u2192 True. Test passes. Lines covered: 28,29,39,40,44,45. \u2713\n\nIn the WORKING world: lines == ['first\\n','second\\n'] asserted. \u2713\n\nOne more thought \u2014 should I ALSO add a strict test expecting Unb