ndLocalError? No \u2014 it would fail in the working world. One robust test only.\n\nHmm, hold on, wait. Let me reconsider AGAIN. I keep flip-flopping. Let me try to settle by probing get_info for the test file's existing content. If the repo's existing tests (which pass) include a stdin test, that tells me the code works. Let me query get_info for likely test names: \"test_islurp\", \"test_islurp_stdin\", \"test_files\". Worth a shot \u2014 cheap.\n\nAlso query \"islurp_url\" to see module context (and confirm get_info works for arbitrary symbols).\n\nLet me do these queries now, then finalize.\n\nActually also: maybe query \"files.islurp\" or \"pytutils.files.islurp\" to see if qualified lookup gives different (fuller) source. Let me batch: get_info(\"test_islurp\"), get_info(\"islurp_url\"), get_info(\"pytutils.files.islurp\").\n\nThen write the final answer.\n\nLet me draft the full test file now (to be adjusted after queries):\n\n```python\nimport io\nimport os\nimport sys\n\nimport pytest\n\nfrom pytutils.files import islurp\n\n\ndef test_islurp_reads_file_line_by_line(tmp_path):\n    path = tmp_path / 'lines.txt'\n    path.write_text('first\\nsecond\\nthird\\n')\n    lines = list(islurp(str(path)))\n    assert lines == ['first\\n', 'second\\n', 'third\\n']\n\n\ndef test_islurp_accepts_linemode_string(tmp_path):\n    path = tmp_path / 'lines.txt'\n    path.write_text('a\\nb\\n')\n    assert list(islurp(str(path), iter_by='LINEMODE')) == ['a\\n', 'b\\n']\n\n\ndef test_islurp_reads_in_chunks(tmp_path):\n    path = tmp_path / 'chunks.txt'\n    path.write_text('abcdefgh')\n    chunks = list(islurp(str(path), iter_by=3))\n    assert chunks == ['abc', 'def', 'gh']\n\n\ndef test_islurp_expands_user(tmp_path, monkeypatch):\n    monkeypatch.setenv('HOME', str(tmp_path))\n    monkeypatch.setenv('USERPROFILE', str(tmp_path))\n    (tmp_path / 'homefile.txt').write_text('from home\\n')\n    assert list(islurp('~/homefile.txt')) == ['from home\\n']\n\n\ndef test_islurp_expa